      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "Copyright 2003 Elsevier Inc. All rights reserved.",
        "AbstractText": "Pain after total hip arthroplasty (THA) may be due to a number of factors, including dysfunction of the iliopsoas tendon. We report a case of persistent groin pain after THA. The pain was successfully treated using iliopsoas tenotomy rather than revision of any prosthetic component."
      },
